{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine","id":1374557,"title":"Have you done cool stuff with Medicine ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-03-13T06:53:14-07:00","id":1374557,"title":"Have you done cool stuff with Medicine ?","content":"Everything's in the title. I'm a bit sad because I usually like Medicinal scenarios where the doctor is at the front, but I've never had an interesting scenario where being a Master Doctor was challenging and felt rewarding.<br /> <br /> Have you examples in your games where Medicine shine beyond &quot;I do 1 roll and it's over let's go to the next part of the game&quot; ? <br /> <br /> Fakeedit : Ok I've actually had one, and it was a character poisoning her leader during Limit Break to take over her place. Was pretty fun and interesting, as the other people were not formed in Medicine so no one understood how all the efforts of the Medic couldn't save the leader.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T07:58:30-07:00","id":1374564,"title":"","content":"Seamstress in my seafaring game was pretty fun. She was a Ghost-Blooded Daybreak Abyssal from Skullstone, and the adopted daughter of the Silver Prince.<br /> <br /> \u200bShe first put her medicinal skills to the test when the crew she served with started coming down with sickness. Once she learned that a tainted water barrel was the source, she dumped out the bad cask and nursed the crew back to health on the first island they reached.<br /> <br /> \u200bLater in the game, a crewman got a hand crushed really badly by a belaying pin after a line was sabotaged by a ghost. Because that crewman had seen these kind of injuries before (and wasn't aware she was an Exalt), he was convinced that the only thing to do was have it amputated; she had to convince him that no, actually, she could restore it to full functionality.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven later, her captain, an Exalt, lost an arm to a combination of a duel with Octavian and taking a brass-banded stone ball (fired from a ballista!) to the elbow. Seamstress ended up cobbling together a necrotech replacement for him out of bits of metal and dead sharks, but because he was being an asshole, she dumped it into the ocean without ever mentioning it, and just used a hearthstone to regenerate his limb. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T08:02:48-07:00","id":1374565,"title":"","content":"I haven\u2019t done it yet hit in my game this summer I have a doctor PC that I\u2019m planning a lot for.<br /> <br /> One of the things to realize is that even Solar doctors can only treat a limited number of sick people in a day or at once. If a town is completely ravaged by plague that\u2019s a LOT more than one roll. You need to prioritize the sickest people, maybe even make some hard choices about how much effort it will take to save some people. You need to institute quarantine to stop the spread of infection and stop people from being reinfected. That means stopping travel in and out of the place as well as sectioning off sick, potentially sick and healthy people.<br /> <br /> You may also be able to treat with a disease god if one is nearby and that disease is within their domain. <br /> <br /> Treating wounded after a battle is similar, you can use Solar medicine to knit bones super fast, but if there\u2019s a ton of people who are risking infection you might want to spread yourself thin just staving off gangrene. <br /> <br /> In either case you\u2019ll want/need assistants to help out, followers or retainers to help tend to the people when you\u2019re off seeing to others. If there\u2019s sabotage your doctor might need to check the medicine you are distributing to make sure it\u2019s not laced with poison or something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T08:17:28-07:00","id":1374568,"title":"","content":"Also keep in mind that even with Flawless Diagnosis Technique, your diagnosis is only as good as the information you're given. If your patient is hiding details from you, your ability to treat his disease might be impacted. Social or investigative skills can help in this regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T09:24:31-07:00","id":1374573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1374568#post1374568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also keep in mind that even with Flawless Diagnosis Technique, your diagnosis is only as good as the information you're given. If your patient is hiding details from you, your ability to treat his disease might be impacted. Social or investigative skills can help in this regard.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I missed something but from my understanding trying to heal someone when you don't know what he has is &quot;just&quot; a -4 or something along those lines. It's quite a malus but for most Solar games I've seen so far no Solar with enough investment in Medicine was never challenged by this kind of stuff. For DB it might come as more interesting though.<br /> <br /> I like as well the idea of investigating and finding secret clues about the ancient sickness that doomed a NPC but I got the feeling players usually went straight for &quot;I do 10 success to heal him&quot; and I quite didn't know where to go from here","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T09:25:39-07:00","id":1374574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1374565#post1374565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven\u2019t done it yet hit in my game this summer I have a doctor PC that I\u2019m planning a lot for.<br /> <br /> One of the things to realize is that even Solar doctors can only treat a limited number of sick people in a day or at once. If a town is completely ravaged by plague that\u2019s a LOT more than one roll. You need to prioritize the sickest people, maybe even make some hard choices about how much effort it will take to save some people. You need to institute quarantine to stop the spread of infection and stop people from being reinfected. That means stopping travel in and out of the place as well as sectioning off sick, potentially sick and healthy people.<br /> <br /> You may also be able to treat with a disease god if one is nearby and that disease is within their domain.<br /> <br /> Treating wounded after a battle is similar, you can use Solar medicine to knit bones super fast, but if there\u2019s a ton of people who are risking infection you might want to spread yourself thin just staving off gangrene.<br /> <br /> In either case you\u2019ll want/need assistants to help out, followers or retainers to help tend to the people when you\u2019re off seeing to others. If there\u2019s sabotage your doctor might need to check the medicine you are distributing to make sure it\u2019s not laced with poison or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I also noticed that &quot;virulent disease&quot; usually don't imply Medicine as much as it implies Bureaucracy and Followers, and I wasn't sure how to bring back the Medicine in this to make the medicinal guy shine","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T09:32:06-07:00","id":1374576,"title":"","content":"I once used Medicine and a fact introduction to solve a medical mystery laid out for my character by a clever ST, and shortly afterward made a somewhat conventional series of extended rolls to represent treating a number of patients in a short time (and managed to save all of them). The mystery was the more intriguing bit, and was a very fun use of Medicine for my character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T09:47:29-07:00","id":1374580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1374576#post1374576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I once used Medicine and a fact introduction to solve a medical mystery laid out for my character by a clever ST, and shortly afterward made a somewhat conventional series of extended rolls to represent treating a number of patients in a short time (and managed to save all of them). The mystery was the more intriguing bit, and was a very fun use of Medicine for my character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh that's cool I totally didn't think about an Extended roll for numerous patients, I don't know how I could miss that. Thanks for the idea, I might re-use it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T10:19:16-07:00","id":1374588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1374573#post1374573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like as well the idea of investigating and finding secret clues about the ancient sickness that doomed a NPC but I got the feeling players usually went straight for &quot;I do 10 success to heal him&quot; and I quite didn't know where to go from here</div> </div> </div> </div>That...yeah that\u2019s an issue. One person no matter how sick is pretty trivial for a Solar to fix, it\u2019s only when like dozens of people are on the verge of death that they really have to flex.<br /> <br /> You could also introduce a magical disease that requires a very specific herb to cure maybe, but then getting that herb may not require medicine so much as survival and stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1374574#post1374574\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I also noticed that &quot;virulent disease&quot; usually don't imply Medicine as much as it implies Bureaucracy and Followers, and I wasn't sure how to bring back the Medicine in this to make the medicinal guy shine</div> </div> </div> </div>Bureaucracy can be good for the organizing part, but ultimately somebody needs to do the administering of aid and for the worst cases that needs to be a legendary healer. Plague, for instance, has a morbidity of 5, which means even somebody with an outstanding 10 dice to the roll still fails 50% of the time to lower their symptoms. Stopping the spread of disease by organizing triage centres and getting people to a place where they can be treated is the job of the bureaucracy Supernal Eclipse, but actually healing them requires medicine. A town of 500 might be experiencing an outbreak of Plague, for example, and 30 people may be infected. You might have to calm the population down with social rolls, organize them to deal with containment with bureaucracy rolls, and then go about actually implementing that plan.<br /> <br /> The Solar Doctor will first have to diagnose anyone not obviously suffering from plague, but suspected to have it so they can separate out the actually infectious people. Flawless Diagnosis Technique is going to do serious work in that case. Next she has to go about actually curing the people, which for each one requires a medicine roll every day of at least 5 successes, but there are only so many motes to go around and only so much time. Each patient requiring an hour, unless you start using Instant Treatment Methodology, which you might have to do if somebody is right on the verge of death and doesn\u2019t have even an hour left. <br /> <br /> Combine all of that together and the only people that have any hope of saving everyone is a truly master Solar doctor. Basically Solars have the power to fight Hell, so put them through Hell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T10:30:05-07:00","id":1374591,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1374573#post1374573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I missed something but from my understanding trying to heal someone when you don't know what he has is &quot;just&quot; a -4 or something along those lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>The way I run things, you do have to declare <i>what</i> you're trying to treat with Medicine. Sometimes, that's obvious - if your Dawn has just taken a daiklave strike to the chest, and is now trying to breathe through her ribcage instead of her throat, well, soaking the penalty for not completely diagnosing all the injuries in favor of just getting on with fixing the immediate problem makes sense. But if you just go ahead and treat the person with the hacking cough and fever without diagnosing them, you'll clear up the bad cold they had, sure... but they'll still die of the lung cancer they had in a few months.<br /> <br /> As to the original question, I don't have cool Medicine stories for my <i>own</i> character (I ST, and I don't get to play much), but one of my players is currently running a Twilight Medicine Supernal. So far, Doctor Hargrave has stitched up more than his fair share of grievous wounds and staved off diseases, including treating a whole manse-full of people for tuberculosis. But the coolest moment for him was, in my opinion, when he found a copy of the Black Treatise on necromancy and, wanting to take the fastest route into initiating into it possible, followed the procedure the book outlined, which involved cutting off someone's arm and replacing it with a corpse arm - and did it all on <i>himself</i>, working with someone to hold the mirror for him.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T10:56:20-07:00","id":1374595,"title":"","content":"The Black Treatise isn't a necromancy book - it's a companion piece to the White Treatise. Where the White Treatise instructs the reader in the methods of sorcery, the Black Treatise instructs in the <i>spells</i>, such as Demon of the First Circle, Death of Obsidian Butterflies, and Stormwind Rider.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T11:37:27-07:00","id":1374602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1374595#post1374595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Black Treatise isn't a necromancy book - it's a companion piece to the White Treatise.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in my version. I didn't look up the details before putting them in the game, but I was basically using the breakdown that the 2e book used. Even if I had looked it up, I would probably have still used the White Treatise as the sorcery book, and the Black Treatise for necromancy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T12:23:01-07:00","id":1374609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1374588#post1374588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bureaucracy can be good for the organizing part, but ultimately somebody needs to do the administering of aid and for the worst cases that needs to be a legendary healer. Plague, for instance, has a morbidity of 5, which means even somebody with an outstanding 10 dice to the roll still fails 50% of the time to lower their symptoms. Stopping the spread of disease by organizing triage centres and getting people to a place where they can be treated is the job of the bureaucracy Supernal Eclipse, but actually healing them requires medicine. A town of 500 might be experiencing an outbreak of Plague, for example, and 30 people may be infected. You might have to calm the population down with social rolls, organize them to deal with containment with bureaucracy rolls, and then go about actually implementing that plan.<br /> <br /> The Solar Doctor will first have to diagnose anyone not obviously suffering from plague, but suspected to have it so they can separate out the actually infectious people. Flawless Diagnosis Technique is going to do serious work in that case. Next she has to go about actually curing the people, which for each one requires a medicine roll every day of at least 5 successes, but there are only so many motes to go around and only so much time. Each patient requiring an hour, unless you start using Instant Treatment Methodology, which you might have to do if somebody is right on the verge of death and doesn\u2019t have even an hour left.<br /> <br /> Combine all of that together and the only people that have any hope of saving everyone is a truly master Solar doctor. Basically Solars have the power to fight Hell, so put them through Hell.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem is rather that I have some difficulties handling the &quot;multiple sick people&quot; part. <br /> <br /> The situation is usually the following : There are a group of sick people somewhere of a very potent disease. The Medicine guy wants to save them, so he will ask to roll for diagnosis/healing. I'll allow it, he will roll crazy results, which is fine, but then I don't know how to handle the two following facts : <br /> - Many people are sick and need to be treated <br /> - The Charms and mechanics are oriented towards healing 1 single person per use<br /> <br /> Since asking for the same roll 10 times in a row is boring, I'll usually call for 1 single roll to see how well he treats them. The player gets crazy successes, and then heals everyone, which is a bit unsatisfying because I would like to develop the process but I don't know where to begin and I feel like the system doesn't entice you either. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The way I run things, you do have to declare <i>what</i> you're trying to treat with Medicine. Sometimes, that's obvious - if your Dawn has just taken a daiklave strike to the chest, and is now trying to breathe through her ribcage instead of her throat, well, soaking the penalty for not completely diagnosing all the injuries in favor of just getting on with fixing the immediate problem makes sense. But if you just go ahead and treat the person with the hacking cough and fever without diagnosing them, you'll clear up the bad cold they had, sure... but they'll still die of the lung cancer they had in a few months. </div> </div> </div>That's a possibility. SO basically you can't truly heal someone if you don't find the specific &quot;narrative&quot; element about the infected person. I might go for that as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T20:05:05-07:00","id":1374696,"title":"","content":"It takes five minutes to Profile a character, and fifteen minutes to treat them. Even if you don't actually play out the conversation, medicine is a great chance to get to know NPCs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2223-ketrus","name":"Ketrus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"398"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-13T21:49:57-07:00","id":1374702,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d just like to point out that <i>any</i> part of the system is going to be boring if all you have it amount to is, \u201croll dice at it.\u201d Even the heady rush of battling to the death is not as exciting if the ST can\u2019t be arsed to figure out why the characters are fighting. Engage the players first, and then use the roll to develop the result of their engagement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T03:24:50-07:00","id":1374732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1374702#post1374702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019d just like to point out that <i>any</i> part of the system is going to be boring if all you have it amount to is, \u201croll dice at it.\u201d Even the heady rush of battling to the death is not as exciting if the ST can\u2019t be arsed to figure out why the characters are fighting. Engage the players first, and then use the roll to develop the result of their engagement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes but for the fighting and social system there are tons of examples and mechanics that goes together that helps flesh out the action and the stakes of what's happening, but I'm having a much harder time with medicine because I feel like even the player doesnt necessarily have a better idea than &quot;I see a wall I climb over it&quot; and we have a hard time finding some implications that goes beyond rhe roll","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T07:06:41-07:00","id":1374750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1374580#post1374580\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh that's cool I totally didn't think about an Extended roll for numerous patients, I don't know how I could miss that. Thanks for the idea, I might re-use it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Specifically, the way it worked was that I had X number of patients to treat and was allowed to make X number of rolls, specifically the same number as the number of patients. Each patient needed Y number of successes to succeed. I could expend multiple rolls on a single patient if I couldn't get the successes all in one roll for him, but that meant there would be patients who went untreated and would presumably die. This was a very tense series of rolls as a result, and when my character ended up saving all the patients, it felt like a huge triumph. I admittedly blew through a ton of motes and had to spend strategically to avoid going all Anima Flux on patients and nurses, but it was a victory well-earned.<br /> <br /> Also to clarify on the &quot;medical mystery&quot;---it was more a mystery that was solved <i>with</i> medical skill rather than a mystery about solving a medical problem. I definitely would recommend trying to give medicine-heavy characters similar chances to contribute to the solving of a problem that is itself not wholly doctoring-based. Perhaps they learn something from a patient they're treating, or they assist in an investigation as a medical examiner, or their skills gain them respect or goodwill from an important party that can further character/group aims, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T07:39:18-07:00","id":1374756,"title":"","content":"Two of my PCs have an ongoing project involving a child who came into the world in similar circumstances to the Striga in the Witcher books/game/tv series correcting multiple deformaties with Wholeness-Restoring Meditation and teaching an essentially feral child how to interact with people again.<br /> <br /> Along the same lines, my Daybreak recently met a bunch of swamp-dwelling cultists who has a practice of grafting animal parts to themselves via thaumaturgy. She's sat in one one of these surgeries and is interested in doing something similar herself though her plan is to give new limbs to soldiers and sailors who've suffered career ending injuries and recruit them into an elite force called the Reforged.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 03-14-2020, 06:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-14T09:23:07-07:00","id":1374768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1374750#post1374750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Specifically, the way it worked was that I had X number of patients to treat and was allowed to make X number of rolls, specifically the same number as the number of patients. Each patient needed Y number of successes to succeed. I could expend multiple rolls on a single patient if I couldn't get the successes all in one roll for him, but that meant there would be patients who went untreated and would presumably die. This was a very tense series of rolls as a result, and when my character ended up saving all the patients, it felt like a huge triumph. I admittedly blew through a ton of motes and had to spend strategically to avoid going all Anima Flux on patients and nurses, but it was a victory well-earned.<br /> <br /> Also to clarify on the &quot;medical mystery&quot;---it was more a mystery that was solved <i>with</i> medical skill rather than a mystery about solving a medical problem. I definitely would recommend trying to give medicine-heavy characters similar chances to contribute to the solving of a problem that is itself not wholly doctoring-based. Perhaps they learn something from a patient they're treating, or they assist in an investigation as a medical examiner, or their skills gain them respect or goodwill from an important party that can further character/group aims, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes I might need to talk more about the circumstances of the sickness and let the medical skills solve this. I have enough general culture to create and let the characters explore new ideas on lots of topics about the rest of the game, but for some reason, even though I watched quite a bit of Dr House, I still feel I have no idea on how to create engaging mystery about a medical subject. Maybe moving from &quot;What is the mystery about the sickness&quot; to &quot;What is the mystery about the people that contracted the sickness&quot; will help me solve this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T00:09:25-07:00","id":1375398,"title":"","content":"In my experience medicine shows up in Exalted games less than it logically should. It's weird with the incentives they created for Ex3 crafting that someone playing a doctor basically has to hope they'll stumble across sick and wounded people over the course of the story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T11:14:20-07:00","id":1375458,"title":"","content":"Rolling against a defenseless static number is just not enjoyable, I wish Medicine has a small sub-system like Lore since currently I feel like a thirsty bottom who has to do 99% of the work to make the night fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T15:36:40-07:00","id":1375499,"title":"","content":"Failing to be 'creative' with medicine in Exalted should be a crime<br /> <br /> Failing at interogating someone? Cue very dubious application of solar medicine charms for very unnecesary amputations. Quadroplegics tend to talk if that's how they get their limbs back.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or there's the lovely one-two- combo with martial arts where you punch out someone's teeth with one fist, then &quot;punch&quot; them back into their mouth with your other fist.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for flaw diagnosis technique and patients lying or witholding info - then you can supplement with investigation charms for that. Always go full Dr. House.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> IIRC there is a 2nd ed solar medicine charm that lets you 'implant' mutations into others. With that you can mess with people a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-18T20:09:28-07:00","id":1375535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1374564#post1374564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seamstress ended up cobbling together a necrotech replacement for him out of bits of metal and dead sharks, but because he was being an asshole, she dumped it into the ocean without ever mentioning it</div> </div> </div> </div>I know it's from back at the beginning of the thread, but this is one of the most quintessentially Exalted things I've read in a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/456-blackwell","name":"Blackwell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar456_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"977"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T02:03:12-07:00","id":1375565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1375499#post1375499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Failing to be 'creative' with medicine in Exalted should be a crime<br /> <br /> Failing at interogating someone? Cue very dubious application of solar medicine charms for very unnecesary amputations. Quadroplegics tend to talk if that's how they get their limbs back.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or there's the lovely one-two- combo with martial arts where you punch out someone's teeth with one fist, then &quot;punch&quot; them back into their mouth with your other fist.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for flaw diagnosis technique and patients lying or witholding info - then you can supplement with investigation charms for that. Always go full Dr. House.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> IIRC there is a 2nd ed solar medicine charm that lets you 'implant' mutations into others. With that you can mess with people a lot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually don't like very much torture in my RPGs. Not trigger or anything, but I find it mostly boring and a way to wave around the interesting Social System (or whatever the plot the game has) to instead bring a generic &quot;I very scare you&quot; solution","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T02:08:34-07:00","id":1375568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1375499#post1375499\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Failing to be 'creative' with medicine in Exalted should be a crime</div> </div> </div> </div>I find your post to be in very bad taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 03-19-2020, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T02:34:02-07:00","id":1375570,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s an expression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T07:55:13-07:00","id":1375609,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1375570#post1375570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s an expression.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good Lord, I'm referring to the graphic descriptions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T09:33:37-07:00","id":1375626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1375609#post1375609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good Lord, I'm referring to the graphic descriptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I frankly would ask a player who intends on using their Medicine dots to facilitate torture, to sit down and have a talk with me about expectations, and state plainly that I'm not comfortable with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-19-2020, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T11:54:20-07:00","id":1375661,"title":"","content":"One aspect of medicine that can be overlooked is \u201cwhere is the disease coming from?\u201d For example, if lots of people in the area are contracting Cholera, there\u2019s probably an issue with their water source. Plague is transmitted by fleas and ticks. And so on. Figuring out and fixing that aspect of the problem could add some nice texture to a medical situation and give the non-doctor PCs something to do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T12:22:55-07:00","id":1375665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1375609#post1375609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good Lord, I'm referring to the graphic descriptions.</div> </div> </div> </div>...Yes, duh.<br /> <br /> One of them <i>did</i> just remind me though how much fun I realized ages ago you can have with Wound-Cleansing Meditation given how getting your arm chopped off in the first place usually works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T12:34:32-07:00","id":1375667,"title":"","content":"The biggest issue I see with using amputation to gain leverage via wholeness-restoration is that your target would need to believe that your promise to heal them if they cooperate was actually worth anything, and, well your willingness to cut someone up is kind of a red flag for them trusting you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 03-20-2020, 08:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T12:55:19-07:00","id":1375674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1375661#post1375661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One aspect of medicine that can be overlooked is \u201cwhere is the disease coming from?\u201d For example, if lots of people in the area are contracting Cholera, there\u2019s probably an issue with their water source. Plague is transmitted by fleas and ticks. And so on. Figuring out and fixing that aspect of the problem could add some nice texture to a medical situation and give the non-doctor PCs something to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>As someone else sort of suggested, I wonder if a simili-&quot;State a fact&quot; could make sense for Medicine for characters to shine in an interesting way","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-20T07:28:10-07:00","id":1375806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1374609#post1374609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem is rather that I have some difficulties handling the &quot;multiple sick people&quot; part.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the game doesn't feature Patient Groups like it features Battle Groups.<br /> <br /> Performance actions at least let you direct social influence at entire groups at once with a single dice-roll action. But you cannot direct a single Medicine action at an entire group of people at once, following the rules as written.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T13:15:12-07:00","id":1375997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1375565#post1375565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I actually don't like very much torture in my RPGs. Not trigger or anything, but I find it mostly boring and a way to wave around the interesting Social System (or whatever the plot the game has) to instead bring a generic &quot;I very scare you&quot; solution</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> as a fancy way of stunting an interogation roll, I find that it works just fine","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T13:17:22-07:00","id":1375998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1375568#post1375568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I find your post to be in very bad taste.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> the solar medical charm that lets you add mutations to people can be used/abused in ways that'll make anything taste good<br /> <br /> Case in point, a player of mine had a twilight solar who was into transhumanism - tried to mutate himself, mixing it up with the charm that sped up medical treatments. He forgot to anethetize himself, and then botched the int+med roll. He ended up able to eat rocks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T17:26:58-07:00","id":1376037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1375997#post1375997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">as a fancy way of stunting an interogation roll, I find that it works just fine</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you considered the possibility that torture is something of a contentious subject for a number of people?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T20:36:42-07:00","id":1376062,"title":"","content":"Again, what about applying Battle Group logic?<br /> <br /> Granted, it works best when the entire cohort of patients is suffering from the same ailment, like poison from their shared water supply, a communal disease, or the sword-wounds inflicted upon them when they tried to fight a single Exalt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-21T22:20:38-07:00","id":1376068,"title":"","content":"I wouldn\u2019t permit a Medicine Charm to <i>heal</i> Magnitude damage on a battle group (especially given that Magnitude damage is an abstraction for lost morale <i>as well as</i> casualties and injuries), but I\u2019d probably permit a high-Essence Medicine Charm to grant phantom Magnitude levels to a battle group, with the Charm that grants extra -0s to a patient as its prerequisite, and with a similar sort of cost to Tiger-Warrior Training Technique or Sea Devil Training Technique.<br /> <br /> I was working with Seamstress\u2019 player on one such Charm during my seafaring game, representing her character drilling the sailors in sanitary practices.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 03-22-2020, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T02:41:07-07:00","id":1376086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1376062#post1376062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, what about applying Battle Group logic?<br /> <br /> Granted, it works best when the entire cohort of patients is suffering from the same ailment, like poison from their shared water supply, a communal disease, or the sword-wounds inflicted upon them when they tried to fight a single Exalt.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I'd work with it, going with some extended roll of medicine with results depending on the success and the Charms available to the character. I would then save up some &quot;special case&quot; NPC for more individual rolls in order to have a chance to bring some drama and revelations. Really good suggestions from everyone here so thank you","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T08:16:55-07:00","id":1376115,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1376068#post1376068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn\u2019t permit a Medicine Charm to <i>heal</i> Magnitude damage on a battle group (especially given that Magnitude damage is an abstraction for lost morale <i>as well as</i> casualties and injuries), but I\u2019d probably permit a high-Essence Medicine Charm to grant phantom Magnitude levels to a battle group, with the Charm that grants extra -0s to a patient as its prerequisite.<br /> <br /> I was working with Seamstress\u2019 player on one such Charm during my seafaring game, representing her character drilling the sailors in sanitary practices.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't thinking of healing magnitude damage in the first place, but I agree with your ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T11:26:50-07:00","id":1376125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1376037#post1376037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you considered the possibility that torture is something of a contentious subject for a number of people?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That sounds a lot more like a matter to be taken up between the ST and the players long before a game even starts. I've never ever had trouble with players starting to complain about the content of the game mid-game, because I always talk with my players first to agree on what kind of tone and level of intensity the game is to have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T11:53:43-07:00","id":1376128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1376125#post1376125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds a lot more like a matter to be taken up between the ST and the players long before a game even starts.</div> </div> </div> </div>You and I <i>aren't </i><i>playing</i> a game right now - you popped into a thread about Medicine and advocated using the Ability to facilitate supernatural torture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T13:07:11-07:00","id":1376142,"title":"","content":"The thing to me is more that it doesn't push forward the Medicine guy to solve problems but rather make something a bit creepy out of an already solvable situation","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-22T19:20:38-07:00","id":1376197,"title":"","content":"What about something like this? It's the story of a plague god that wants to start a great cult to himself, deciding that the first step as an abject lesson is to send one of his priests to a town to demand tribute or face the wrath of the plague. If they refuse destroy the town with a plague and continue on to the next one, using the first town to emphasize the threat. At the start of the first day two people are suffering from defining symptoms, one in the lords fort and another in the village, three are suffering from major sympoms and another six from minor symptoms.<br /> <br /> The local people have, generally, a defining principle of &quot;Family comes first&quot;, a major tie of Loyalty towards the rulers of Okawa, Laian and her husband Gema &quot;The Toad&quot;, a minor tie of faith for the Immaculate Order, and a minor tie of mistrust towards outsiders after a strange outsider passed by recently. They also have a resolve and guile of 1 base.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 1 Uncovering Something is Wrong In Okawa village</b><br /> <br /> The characters happen upon a town and something odd may be happening there. A successful (Perception + Socialize or Medicine) check of difficulty 3 will reveal to the players that there is an illness in the town. Either by how people are acting, or the few people who are out with mild symptoms. While this will reveal that there is an illness, it will not reveal what.<br /> <br /> If one of the sick people allows themselves to be investigated a difficulty 3 diagnosis roll will identify the victim as suffering from plague. If a character has been able to examine a character suffering at the defining level reduce the difficulty to 1. From now on any close contact with an infected person counts as exposure to plague, with the modification that the plague is Virulence 5, due to the plague god boosting it with Contagion-Honing Methodology.<br /> <br /> From here players are likely going to want to either see the rulers of Okawa, or just start setting up medical treatment. If the former proceed to scene 3, if the later proceed to scene 2.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 2 Gathering the People</b><br /> <br /> The people of Okawa must be kept separated in quarantine, expect for those infected by the plague who require medical treatment as soon as possible. Telling them all of this is difficult however as they are untrusting of outsiders, and are resistant to any of them telling them what to do. Also large gatherings where people can be told things en masse are dangerous during an epidemic, if such a gathering occurs add one additional infected person for each already infected.<br /> <br /> There are some people who may help spread the word around town, but they must be convinced first. Asking them to do so is considered a major task as it involves completely disrupting the functioning of the town. The local leaders who might do this are a touch more savvy than the normal mortals and have a resolve and guile of 2. Once cooperation has been secured scene 4 becomes available to go to.<br /> <br /> Either way, at the end of this scene if the players have not already been to the hill fort the watch captain and four of her guards come to escort the players there for scene 3. Use Champion and Battle Ready Troops for them respectively. If the players choose to kill the guards instead the entire town will turn on them and disaster follows.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 3 Meeting Laian and the Toad</b><br /> <br /> Atop a nearby hill rests the Fort Okawa, where the Toad and his wife administer to the village of Okawa as well as four other nearby towns. It is an old structure, dating back 300 years and built by the Realm when it took Okawa as a satrapy for House Tepet. The satrap herself lives in a palace in the capital city several days journey from Okawa. For both Laian and the Toad use the stats for the Snakefolk merchant, without the poisonous bite. They also have a defining principle that the area they rule is both their property and under their protection, a major principle of faith in the Immaculate Order, a major tie of love for their son, and a minor tie of love for eachother.<br /> <br /> They also have a secret, their young son they believe, was one of the first to be infected by the plague. After the priest of the plague god was brought into an audience with them and they refused his tribute, threatening to bring the Immaculate monks down on him, he left and their son immediately became ill. Prying that secret out of them will take some effort however.<br /> <br /> Also convincing them to stop travel between the villages and allow treatment of Okawa to stop the spread of plague is a major task. If they allow the players to see their son he is on the verge of death, suffering from the defining symptoms of plague, that night make the roll for him to survive or fail. If he dies the lord and lady fall into a depression and are even more difficult to rouse to action.<br /> <br /> Laian is also aware that her huntswoman, a person named Tamara, has gone missing in the woods outside of Okawa. Finding her requires tracking a trail of difficulty 5 through the woods, as it has been intentionally hidden by forest spirits loyal to the plague god. Proceed to scene 6 if that is what the players do.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 4 Administering Triage</b><br /> <br /> With everyone safely quarantining at home, only those who suspect they are sick gather at a place determined by the players. This place should be sheltered and spacious if they can secure it. Here all the infected people gather for treatment. Determining proper treatment is an (Intelligence + Medicine) roll of difficulty 3, given the less than desirable circumstances of a barn or the like. once those have been implemented the people with minor symptoms will begin to recover, but those with major and defining will still deteriorate without medical attention.<br /> <br /> The one person suffering from defining symptoms is actually dragged into the triage center by guards, she is suffering from Blight Decree and desperate to roam the town touching everything she can. Treating her is done at a -3 die penalty as she constantly fights against the treatment. A successful (Intelligence + Occult) roll of difficulty 2 reveals to the player that this may be the result of Blight Decree, and that the plague god may still be active in the town.<br /> <br /> The plague god can either be found by tracking down his priest, who is on the road to the next town or near the sanctum of the god, or by finding it lurking at the edge of the town using occult charms and forcing/convincing it to materialize.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 5 Confronting the Plague God</b><br /> <br /> The plague god materializes in a miasma of foul smelling clouds. Use the stats for a disease spirit except change its essence to 4 and grant it an additional health level at each penalty level. Also its Festering Revelation charm affects 4 people instead of 1, and requires no attack roll as roiling cloud of disease extends from its wretched fingers. Five hundred years ago it was imprisoned by a Dragonblood using Anathema Sealing Tomb, and at last it has freed itself.<br /> <br /> It has a defining principle that it is powerful and worthy of worship, another defining principle that plague must be spread to the corners of Creation, a major principle of hatred for the Dragonblooded, and a minor tie of wistful fondness for the woods that its sanctum is in.<br /> <br /> The players may engage it in combat, although if they slay it without doing so permanently it reforms in its nearby sanctum, a cave beneath a hill in the forest. Otherwise if the god feels it is losing or finds it is outmatched it retreats using hurry home. Convincing it to remove its disease blessing and promoting charms is a Life-Changing task.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 6 The Sanctum Entrance</b><br /> <br /> If the players decide to track down the god at its sanctum, perhaps it's fled there after a confrontation. Outside the cave is a dying woman, in the last stages of the plague she sits propped up against a rock. She had gone to the woods to investigate the local game situation, but ran into the priest of the plague god. Falling for a trick of his where he asked for her aid in rescuing his supposedly lost daughter in the cave, she was pushed into a fetid pool and nearly drowned. Pulling herself out she awakened an unknown amount of time later weakened and appearingly suffering from some disease. She has survived this long by eating nearby plantlife and drinking shallow pools of water, too weak to return home.<br /> <br /> In fact it is not a disease at all but poison fermented in the water. Treat it as arcenic, having already filled her to her last -2 health level over the preceeding days and with 5 days still left on the duration. Treating it is a difficulty 3 roll under Treating Poisons on page 237.<br /> <br /> She gives a valuable warning though, for in the cave there are spirits that would drown the PCs. There are five spirits, flickerfeathers, hiding in that cave near the water. They're hiding among the rocks in the pitch blackness of the deep cave, and use their mimicry to try and lure people closer to the water's edge where they can catch them and drag them down. All physical and visual actions take a -1 penalty due to rough slippery terrain, and increased to -3 without bright proper lighting.<br /> <br /> They may just pester the players, or lead them in a chase around the cave where they're liable to slip and fall into the pool without proper athletics rolls. Once they have been dealt with one way or another the players may then attempt an occult ritual to open the doorway to the sanctum of the plague god. Doing so requires an hour of work, candles which may be bough in town from the local candlemaker, and an (Intelligence + Occult) roll of difficulty 4.<br /> <br /> Discovering this ritual may require some kind of lore roll, or contact with One River, the immaculate.<br /> <br /> <b>Scene 7 The Sanctum Proper</b><br /> <br /> The sanctum of the disease god is much like the cave that lead to it. With the exception that it leads out to a rotten, diseased version of the same forest the players have just left. Here are some of the plague god's new allies. Taking whatever it can get at first, and lowering itself to sealing from the elemental spirit courts, several Greenmaws wend their way through this forest. If the players seek to confront the god here in combat the greenmaws join it.<br /> <br /> After the god is slain or convinced to reverse the effects of its blight on the town the disease can be cleaned up relatively easily.<br /> <br /> <b>Wildcard One River</b><br /> <br /> Wandering through the Okawa region may be the immaculate monk One River. She's a fairly experienced water aspect, who specializes in medicine and abhors combat, although she is proficient in Water Dragon Style she practices it more for spiritual enlightenment and physical fitness. If encountered by the players she is more than happy to assist with battling this plague and the plague god. If the players are celestial exalted however they must try to keep their natures hidden from her if they want to keep her aid, she has no qualms about fleeing for a Wyld Hunt or outing the players to the local people.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's just a random attempt, it's not really meant to be a usable adventure, and stuff could easily be modified on the fly. Maybe there's a greater conspiracy of disease gods and this is only the start with a minor god, maybe there's an assassination plot trying to poison the rulers, etc. Either way I think going about it like that, with a few really critical cases of the disease, rather than being able to treat whole swaths of the population at once with a charm is a better way to do it. It is an intentional design hole in even Solar medicine that they can't just go into a city and snap their fingers to fix a plague.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-23T08:21:35-07:00","id":1376263,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1374557-have-you-done-cool-stuff-with-medicine?p=1375661#post1375661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One aspect of medicine that can be overlooked is \u201cwhere is the disease coming from?\u201d For example, if lots of people in the area are contracting Cholera, there\u2019s probably an issue with their water source. Plague is transmitted by fleas and ticks. And so on. Figuring out and fixing that aspect of the problem could add some nice texture to a medical situation and give the non-doctor PCs something to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh wow. That sounds like epidemiology. I'm studying it right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}